      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Pain is a common and feared problem for those with advanced cancer. The goal of palliative care is to relieve suffering and improve quality of life. A step-by-step approach allows good symptom management and minimisation of drug side effects."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "This article aims to improve the general practitioner's confidence in prescribing in the palliative care setting and to encourage early involvement of community palliative care teams."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "DISCUSSION",
          "content": "Opioid initiation and substitution, and the role of other medications and nondrug therapies in controlling cancer pain are discussed."
        }
      ]},
